chapter.v:
For if 


God did, 


not spare angels when they sinned, but cast them into hell(1) and committed them to chains(2) of gloomy darkness to be kept until the judgment;

if he 


did not, 


spare the ancient world, but preserved Noah, a herald of righteousness, with seven others, when he brought a flood upon the world of the ungodly;

(for as 


that righteous, 


man lived among them day after day, he was tormenting his righteous soul over their lawless deeds that he saw and heard);
